A fantasy symbol/emblem design. A key broken cleanly in two halves, separated by a small gap. The key is ornate, medieval style, with a circular bow (top) and a simple ward (teeth). The two halves are slightly offset as if pulled apart. Engraved in stone or drawn on aged parchment. No color, monochrome, like a bas-relief carving or an ink stamp. Style: clean symbol illustration suitable for a D&D handout, parchment background, simple and iconic.
